  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "A computer can do \\(10{,}000\\) additions per second. How many additions can it do in one hour?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\) million",
    "B": "\\(36\\) million",
    "C": "\\(60\\) million",
    "D": "\\(216\\) million",
    "E": "\\(360\\) million"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The computer's rate is given per second, so first express one hour in seconds. There are \\(60\\) minutes in an hour and \\(60\\) seconds in each minute, giving\n\\[60\\cdot60=3600\\text{ seconds}.\\]\nAt \\(10000\\) additions each second, the total is\n\\[10000\\cdot3600=36000000\\text{ additions}.\\]\nThis is \\(36\\) million additions, choice B.",
